# REDCOVER WEB PLATFORM
## MASTER PRODUCT REQUIREMENTS, UI/UX DESIGN SYSTEM, TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE AND DEVELOPMENT SPECIFICATION

---

# PART 1: PROJECT IDENTITY AND VISION

## 1.1 Project Name

Redcover

Tagline: Read • Write • Share • Connect

## 1.2 Project Overview

Redcover is a modern digital reading, publishing, book discovery, and social networking platform.

The platform brings together readers, independent authors, writers, publishers, and communities in one ecosystem.

Users should be able to:

- Discover interesting books.
- Read books online.
- Upload their own PDF books.
- Write and publish original stories.
- Follow authors and other readers.
- Build friendships.
- Communicate through direct messaging.
- Review and rate books.
- Save books to personal libraries.
- Track reading progress.
- Participate in a reading community.
- Earn points and maintain reading streaks.
- Access premium membership features.

An existing Android application called Redcover is already developed.

The objective is to build a professional web version of this same platform.

This is NOT a separate product.

It is another client of the existing Redcover ecosystem.

## 1.3 Core Product Philosophy

Redcover should feel like a combination of:

- A premium online bookstore.
- A digital ebook reader.
- A publishing platform.
- A social network for readers.
- A community for independent writers.

The interface must prioritize reading, discovery, publishing, and community engagement.

The website should feel professional, trustworthy, modern, lightweight, and visually attractive.

## 1.4 Target Users

The website should support:

1. Casual readers who discover books.
2. Regular readers who maintain reading lists.
3. Independent writers who publish stories.
4. Authors who manage their books and audiences.
5. Readers who interact with other readers.
6. Premium members.
7. Platform administrators.

